    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: optional owner `email`\n\nThe requirement \u2014 an owner may include `email`; when present it must be a syntactically valid address, stored and returned lower-cased; reject with 400 when present but invalid \u2014 is satisfied end-to-end.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added an optional `email` string property to the `OwnerFields` schema (not in `required`), so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain `getEmail`/`setEmail`.\n\n2. **Owner entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added an `email` column with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it to/from the DTOs automatically by name.\n\n3. **Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) \u2014 added a `normalizeEmail(...)` helper mirroring the existing `normalizeTelephone` idiom:\n   - blank/absent \u2192 left as-is (optional field, accepted);\n   - present but not matching a syntactic email pattern \u2192 throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"email\"])`, which the existing advice maps to **400**;\n   - valid \u2192 lower-cased before storing.\n   \n   Applied in both `addOwner` (create) and `updateOwner`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a nullable `email` column to `owners` in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and updated the positional seed `INSERT`s (hsqldb, mysql) to include the new column so schema init still succeeds. Tests run on the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required.\n\n**Tests:** the suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` (3 tests: lower-casing, invalid\u2192400, missing-email accepted) passes, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nOne design note: validation/normalization lives in the controller (matching the existing `telephone` pattern) rather than as a bean-validation `@Email` annotation, since the lower-casing has to happen there anyway and this keeps the rule in a single place.",
